W: 1 The day is past and over;
W: all thanks, O Lord, to thee;
W: I pray thee that sinless
W: the hours of dark may be:
W: O Jesu, keep me in thy sight,
W: and guard me through the coming night.
W:
W: 2 The joys of day are over;
W: I lift my heart to thee,
W: and ask thee that offenceless
W: the hours of dark may be:
W: O Jesu, keep me in thy sight,
W: and guard me through the coming night.
W:
W: 3 The toils of day are over;
W: I lift my heart to thee,
W: and ask that free from peril
W: the hours of dark may be:
W: O Jesu, keep me in thy sight,
W: and guard me through the coming night.
W:
W: 4 Be thou my soul&apos;s preserver,
W: for thou alone dost know
W: how many are the perils
W: through which I have to go:
W: O loving Jesu, hear my call,
W: and guard and save me from them all.
W:</miscellaneous-field>
